{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"vampiric-dollfaced-aurochs","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Discovered from bug e548-5b35-7eb8-4727 (bolstered-afraid-ichidna)\n\nWhile root-causing e548 it was proven that the failing test is **invisible to CI**, which is how\nthe breaking change earned `Verified +1`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `tests/unit/test_path_injection_guards.py` guards the review-bot test with\n  `pytest.importorskip(\"fastapi\")`. Whole files do the same at module scope, e.g.\n  `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py:20-21`.\n- **No CI lane ever installs fastapi.** All three install steps in\n  `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` (lines 70, 219, 295) run\n  `uv sync --locked --extra dev`. The `dev` extra contains no fastapi (verified by parsing\n  pyproject: `dev has fastapi? False`); fastapi lives only in the `reviewbot` and `ui` extras\n  (`pyproject.toml:93`, `:100`).\n- `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:169` lists the isolation `specs=(...)` as\n  agents / eval / tracing / grounding / metrics / mcp / union — **`reviewbot` is absent** — and\n  that lane runs an import probe only, never pytest.\n- Reproduced: `uv sync --locked --extra dev --extra agents` then running the suite reports\n  `SKIPPED [1] tests/unit/test_path_injection_guards.py:148: could not import 'fastapi'`.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nEvery `rebar.review_bot` and `rebar.opcert_service` test — including SECURITY guards (the\n`/rerun` 502 stack-trace-exposure guard, the `X-Opcert-Guard` 403 auth guard, the 66af token\nredaction suite) — silently no-ops in CI. A change can break all of them and still be\n`Verified +1`. This directly contradicts the stated invariant in the `_optionality.yml:163-168`\ncomment: \"the isolation set is every key of `_optional.EXTRAS` — so a newly declared extra\ncannot ship with ZERO CI\".\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A CI lane installs the `reviewbot` extra and RUNS the tests it unlocks (not just an import probe)\n- [ ] Proven by seeding a deliberate break in a review-bot test and observing CI go red\n- [ ] Consider a guard that fails the build when a `pytest.importorskip` skip is unlocked by no lane","id":"599e-77da-29dd-482d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"review-bot + opcert tests are permanently SKIPPED in CI: no lane installs the reviewbot extra"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786096290682816001,"uuid":"01ff965f-03f1-44f9-981b-1511ed238a04"}